          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8b21f268cce8c7d784775ee3074311498aee18df",
          "message": "fix(reason/n3): bound the compiled-rules evaluator by ClosureLimits (#6934)\n\n* fix(reason/n3): bound the compiled-rules evaluator by ClosureLimits (#6855)\n\nThe opt-in `compiled-rules` evaluator now runs under the text engine's\nClosureLimits: the round and fact allowance (bounded::ClosureRounds) and\nthe term-size checkpoint (bounded::derived_term via refused_term). Each\nbuiltin result (string:concatenation incl. numeric pieces,\nstring:encodeForUri, string:scrape, log:uri both ways) and each `( … )`\nargument list is sized with the text engine's helpers before it is built.\nPast any allowance evaluation returns the text engine's\n\"forward closure limit exceeded\" error instead of a truncated closure or\nan allocation failure.\n\nAPI: compiled::eval / BoundRuleSet::eval now return\nResult<Vec<[Id; 3]>, String>; new eval_with_limits variants take a\nClosureLimits. sparq-solid callers propagate the error. concat_push now\ndelegates its value coercion to the text engine's concat_piece.\n\nTests: compiled_equivalence.rs adds the #6771 doubling repro and sweeps\nmax_term_bytes, max_rounds and max_facts across their boundaries,\nchecking both engines refuse together or return the same closure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ScyGGohDhirnbLbrUSnA5n\n\n* docs(reason/n3): narrow the compiled/text limit parity claim; CHANGELOG Breaking entry (#6855)\n\nBoth engines are bounded by the same ClosureLimits and refuse with the same\nerror, but their fixpoint schedules differ (closing naive round, transitivity\nfast path, quoted-triple substitution checkpoints), so near a boundary they\ncan accept or refuse differently. The rustdoc, SKILL.md and test comments now\nsay the engines agree at the swept limits only. Adds the Breaking CHANGELOG\nentry for compiled::eval / BoundRuleSet::eval returning Result and the new\neval_with_limits variants.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ScyGGohDhirnbLbrUSnA5n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
